This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.

**Before using Read, Grep, Glob, or Bash to explore the codebase, run graphify first:**

- `graphify query "<question>"` — subgraph for architecture/code questions
- `graphify path "A" "B"` — shortest path between two nodes
- `graphify explain "X"` — node plus neighbors

This applies to you and every subagent. Put this rule in subagent prompts that explore code.

Use Read/Grep/Glob directly only when:

1. Graphify already oriented you and you need exact lines to edit
2. `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet

After changing code, run `graphify update .` (AST only, no API key).

Internal product context (gitignored) is **not** in the graph until docs are extracted. Always also read `.internal/rti/README.md` and `.internal/rti/AGENT-LEDGER.md` before implementing.
